ment of marine life. Special-use permits allow experienced divers to explore the reserve. Seals, sea lions and sea otters can be seen in the park's cove. Hikers can discover the park's backcountry via several trail systems.  There is no park kiosk at Julia Pfeiffer Burns State Park for fee collection. Campers should register at Pfeiffer Big Sur State Park or Big Sur Station.  For Special Events in the parks such as weddings and small celebrations, please e-mail Special Events at BigSurEvents@parks.ca.gov.", "HasAlerts": false, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Birdwatching<br>Camping<br>Hiking<br>Picnic area<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=578", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/661.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 36.15892586, "Longitude": -121.6704589, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:15:15", "MilesFromSelected": 9, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": false, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 666, "Name": "Limekiln SP", "Description": "Limekiln State Park contains 716-acres. The park features breath taking views of the Big Sur Coast. The park features the beauty of the redwoods, the rugged coast, and the cultural history of limekilns.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Camping<br>Fishing<br>Hiking<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=577", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/666.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "Pa