f Ponderosa pine. The park has a picnic area above the San Lorenzo River. Anglers fish for steelhead and salmon during the winter. The Park has a nature center, bookstore and campfire center.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Birdwatching<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Museum<br>Picnic area<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=546", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/655.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 37.04010491, "Longitude": -122.0640131, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:15:15", "MilesFromSelected": 57, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 713, "Name": "Hearst San Simeon SP", "Description": "Enjoy the scenic beauty of the Pacific Ocean while camping at San Simeon Creek Campground (water + showers) or Washburn Campground (water fill-up in lower campground + no showers).  This tranquil getaway has many recreational options.   Beach is closed to dogs for the protection of the threatened Snowey Plover shorebird.  ", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Birdwatching<br>Boating<br>Boat launch<br>Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Hiking<br>Picnic area<br>Scuba diving<br>Surfing<br>Swimming<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=590", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/713.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Small", "Latitude": 35.59939284, "Longitude": -121.1254548, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:15:15", "MilesFromSelected": 59, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": false, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 1, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-22T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 10, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 656, "Name": "Henry W Coe SP", "Description": "Henry W. Coe State Park is primarily a wilderness park.  Spring is the most popular time of year to visit with fabulous displays of wildflowers.  Camping is permitted all year.  There are numerous creeks and ponds, ranging from 2 to 22 miles from the Coe Ranch Entrance.  Fishing is allowed in the park; Fish and Game regulations are enforced.  Be prepared to hike or bike on dirt roads and trails.  Vehicle access is restricted beyond park entrances.", "HasAlerts": false, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Birdwatching<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Museum<br>Picnic area<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=561", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/656.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 37.18800496, "Longitude": -121.548013, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:15:15", "MilesFromSelected": 66, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-29T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 30, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 667, "Name": "Little Basin State Park", "Description": "The Little Basin Campground is for group camping for four (4) or more people only. LITTLE BASIN, once a retreat and campground for Hewlett Packard employees, is a 534-acre California State Park campground that was recently added to Big Basin Redwoods State Park through a collaborative endeavor with Peninsula Open Space Trust (POST) and the Sempervirens Fund. Through an innovative approach to park operations and a public/private partnership, Little Basin is managed by Basecamp Hospitality, a recreation and hospitality company that works with California State Parks.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Fire Rings<br>Playground<br>Amphitheater<br>Showers<br>Potable Water<br>Picnic Tables<br>Telephone<br>Ranger Station<br>Hiking Trails<br>Nature Trails<br>Basketball Net-Court<br>Tennis Court<br>Parking<br>Group Picnic Area<br>Restrooms<br>2 Sports Fields<br>Sand Volleyball Court<br>Horseshoe Pit<br>Group Campfire Ring<br>Group BBQ Area<br>", "Url": "http://www.Littlebasin.com", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/667.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Small", "Latitude": 37.15533333, "Longitude": -122.2031667, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:15:15", "MilesFromSelected": 67, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": false, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 1, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 711, "Name": "San Luis Reservoir SRA", "Description": "San Luis Reservoir SRA is nestled in the grassy hills of the western San Joaquin Valley near historic Pacheco Pass. It offers three lakes for fishing, boating, board sailing, camping, and picnicking. The San Luis Reservoir stores runoff water from the Delta that would otherwise flow into the ocean.\r\n", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Birdwatching<br>Boating<br>Boat launch<br>Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Off Road Vehicles<br>Picnic area<br>Rinse Showers<br>Surfing<br>Swimming<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=558", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/711.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "large", "Latitude": 37.03626598, "Longitude": -121.0917829, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:15:15", "MilesFromSelected": 67, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 6, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 3, "Name": "Big Basin Redwoods SP", "Description": "Big Basin Redwoods State Park is the oldest State Park in California.  It was acquired in 1902.  The park has miles of trails, which serves hikers and equestrians, links Big Basin to Castle Rock State Park and the eastern reach of the Santa Cruz range.  The Skyline to the Sea Trail threads its way through the park along Waddell Creek to the ocean.  The park has a surprising number of waterfalls, a wide variety of environments (from lush canyon bottoms to sparse chaparral-covered slopes, many animals (deer, raccoons, an occasional bobcat) and lots of bird life (including Steller's jays, egrets, herons and California woodpeckers). The park is also the home to stately redwood groves.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Camping<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Museum<br>Picnic area<br>Store-convenience<br>Swimming<br>Visitor Center", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=540", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/3.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Small", "Latitude": 37.17290726370264, "Longitude": -122.21154785155761, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:15:15", "MilesFromSelected": 68, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": false, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 1, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 1111, "Name": "Castle Rock SP", "Description": "Castle Rock SP", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Camping<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Picnic area<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=538", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/1111.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Small", "Latitude": 37.2125121, "Longitude": -122.1510811, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:15:15", "MilesFromSelected": 70, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": false, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 30, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 618, "Name": "Big Basin Redwoods  SP Tent Cabins", "Description": "Big Basin Redwoods State Park is located in the beautiful Santa Cruz Mountains among the inspiring California Redwoods. Big Basin Tent Cabins offer convenience and comfort in a beautiful outdoor setting.  Big Basin Tent Cabins feature raised platforms with mattress pads, a table, a wood stove, and a lockable door. There is also a picnic table, fire ring, and room for one traditional tent outside. Best of all, this enclosed structure requires no set-up!  If you do not own any camping gear, try the Total Camping Packages add-on, including 4 sleeping bags, a cook stove, pots and pans, cooking utensils, a lantern, and a 60-quart cooler. Also, one bundle of wood and one bag of ice are provided per night (max of two each per reservation). This package can be reserved online. Cabins available for this package are #8, #9, #20, #28 and #29. The Camping Packages cost $159 per night.  Better still, try our Deluxe Cabins, including your beds made up for your arrival (sheets, towels, blankets, comforter, and pillows), curtains, lantern, bath towels, and washcloths. Deluxe Cabins are available online. Cabins available for this package are #6, #7, #10, #12, #13, #14, #30, and #31. The Deluxe Cabins cost $129 per night.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Comfort Station<br>Showers<br>Toilet, Accessible<br>Dump Station<br>Fire Rings<br>Hiking Trails<br>Parking<br>Ranger Station<br>Picnic Area<br>Visitors Center<br>Nature Trails<br>Store - Convenience<br>Restrooms<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=540", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/618.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 37.214122, "Longitude": -122.242298, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:15:15", "MilesFromSelected": 72, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": false, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 1, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 2, "MaximumStay": 30, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 695, "Name": "Portola Redwoods SP", "Description": "Portola Redwoods State Park has a rugged, natural basin forested with coast redwoods, Douglas fir and live oak. Eighteen miles of trails crisscross the canyon and its two streams, Peters Creek and Pescadero Creek. A short nature trail along Pescadero Creek introduces visitors to the natural history of the area. Visitors can see clam shells and other marine deposits from the time when the area was once covered by the ocean. The park has one of the tallest redwoods (300 feet high) in the Santa Cruz Mountains.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Camping<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Museum<br>Picnic area<br>Swimming<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=539", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/695.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 37.26237292, "Longitude": -122.2123671, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:15:15", "MilesFromSelected": 74, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 681, "Name": "Morro Strand SB", "Description": "Morro Strand State Beach is a three-mile coastal frontage park. From the beach, visitors can view the entire Estero Bay, including Morro Rock. Activities include fishing, surfing, wind and kite surfing, kite flying, sunbathing, strolling on the beach, bird watching, and exploring the town of Morro Bay. ", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Boating<br>Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Horseback riding<br>Picnic area<br>Rinse Showers<br>Surfing<br>Swimming<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=593", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/681.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 35.40199484, "Longitude": -120.8678627, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:15:15", "MilesFromSelected": 78, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": false, "ParkCategoryId": 2, "ParkActivity": 1, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-22T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 10, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 680, "Name": "Morro Bay SP", "Description": "Morro Bay State Park features lagoon and natural bay habitat. The bay's most prominent landmark is Morro Rock. The park has opportunities for sailing fishing, hiking, and bird watching. The park museum has exhibits that cover natural features and cultural history, Native American life, geology, and oceanography. The park also has a colorful marina and an 18-hole public golf course. On the bay's northeast edge is a pristine saltwater marsh that supports a thriving bird population.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Birdwatching<br>Boating<br>Boat launch<br>Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Golf course<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Museum<br>Picnic area<br>Rinse Showers<br>Surfing<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=594", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/680.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Small", "Latitude": 35.34653383, "Longitude": -120.8419937, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:15:15", "MilesFromSelected": 82, "Available": true, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 1, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-22T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 10, "IsRestrictionValid": true, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": true}, {"PlaceId": 679, "Name": "Montana De Oro SP", "Description": "Montana de Oro State Park features over 8,000 acres of rugged cliffs, secluded sandy beaches,\r\n coastal plains, streams, canyons, and hills - with 1,347-foot Valencia Peak. Naturalists and backpackers enjoy the solitude and \r\n freedom found along the park trails. There are also mountain biking and equestrian trails. The best-known beach is Spooner's Cove,\r\n across from the campground. The park's name (Mountain of Gold) comes from the golden wildflowers that bloom in spring.\r\n  Wildlife in the park includes black tailed deer and the black oystercatcher. The park includes primitive and equestrian campsites.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Boating<br>Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Picnic area<br>Scuba diving<br>Surfing<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=592", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/679.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 35.26388889, "Longitude": -120.8622222, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:15:15", "MilesFromSelected": 86, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 1, "ParkActivity": 1, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 648, "Name": "George J. Hatfield SRA", "Description": "George J. Hatfield SRA is located in the San Joaquin Valley and home to a variety of trees and wildlife. The Merced River meanders through the park, with swimming and fishing activities near facilities. It offers spacious grassy fields and picnic tables shaded by native oak trees for day use activities.\r\n", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Boating<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Picnic area<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=556", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/648.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 37.35220501, "Longitude": -120.9610129, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:15:15", "MilesFromSelected": 89, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 6, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 652, "Name": "Half Moon Bay SB", "Description": "Half Moon Bay State Beach is actually four smaller beaches, with a total of two miles of sandy shore. The beach is a popular location for camping, picnicing, surfing, and surf fishing.  Swimming is not recommended.  Visitors enjoy a multi use, coastal trail that runs approximately 4 miles along Half Moon Bay.  A short access trail leading to the beach is less than 100 yards from anywhere in the campground.", "HasAlerts": true, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Bicycling<br>Birdwatching<br>Boating<br>Body surfing<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Horseback riding<br>Picnic area<br>Rinse Showers<br>Surfing<br>Swimming<br>Visitor Center<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=531", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/652.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 37.46650492, "Longitude": -122.4450132, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:15:15", "MilesFromSelected": 92, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 2, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 7, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}, {"PlaceId": 676, "Name": "Mcconnell SRA", "Description": "McConnell State Recreation Area is located on the banks of the Merced River. It offers over 70 acres of outdoor activities for families and fishermen. Spring, summer, and fall offer fishing, camping, picnicking, river wading, sunbathing, hiking and nature study.", "HasAlerts": false, "IsFavourite": false, "Allhighlights": "Boating<br>Camping<br>Fishing<br>Group Camping<br>Hiking<br>Picnic area<br>Rinse Showers<br>Swimming<br>", "Url": "http://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=554", "ImageUrl": "https://cali-content.usedirect.com/Images/California/ParkImages/Place/676.jpg", "BannerUrl": null, "ParkSize": "Medium", "Latitude": 37.41663704, "Longitude": -120.7132969, "TimeZone": "America/Los_Angeles", "TimeStamp": "2026-06-22 13:15:15", "MilesFromSelected": 100, "Available": false, "AvailableFiltered": true, "ParkCategoryId": 6, "ParkActivity": 3, "ParkPopularity": 0, "AvailableUnitCount": 0, "PartialAvailable": false, "Restrictions": {"FutureBookingStarts": "2026-06-24T00:00:00-07:00", "FutureBookingEnds": "2026-12-22T00:00:00-08:00", "MinimumStay": 1, "MaximumStay": 10, "IsRestrictionValid": false, "Time": "0001-01-01T00:00:00"}, "Facilities": {}, "IsAvailableForGreatwalk": false, "IsReservationAnyDrawActive": true, "FacilityDefaultZoom": 13, "IsReservationDrawActive": false}]}, "part": "place-690"}